<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>On Llama-3-8B-Instruct, 30 randomly selected instances from the NarrativeQA dataset are used to perform EvolKV layer-wise KV cache budget optimization at <math id="A3.T8.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=128</annotation></semantics></math> three times to evaluate stability.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Comparison Results of Different Selection of Training Data for Optimization</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present in Table <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ C.3 Comparison Results of Different Selection of Training Data for Optimization ‣ Appendix C Detailed Results of Analysis ‣ EvolKV: Evolutionary KV Cache Compression for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> the results of EvolKV optimized with different training data configurations. The training data consists of two settings: the single-multi doc set, comprising 30 examples sampled from the single- and multi-document QA categories, and the six-subsets set, constructed from samples drawn from six datasets—NarrativeQA, HotpotQA, QMSum, TREC, PassageRetrieval-en, and LCC. The optimized results suggest that EvolKV holds a performance advantage, indicating its potential to maintain effective results across diverse downstream training data and demonstrating its strong adaptability.</p>
</div>
