<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Comparison results of optimization and expansion. ".ex" denotes using the budget allocation optimized at <math id="A3.T10.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=128</annotation></semantics></math> to expand to target average KV cache budgets <math id="A3.T10.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>; ".opt" denotes using EvolKV optimization at the corresponding <math id="A3.T10.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Transfer Results of KV Cache Budget Optimization to Other Datasets</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ C.5 Transfer Results of KV Cache Budget Optimization to Other Datasets ‣ Appendix C Detailed Results of Analysis ‣ EvolKV: Evolutionary KV Cache Compression for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> presents the evaluation results on the LongBench benchmark by directly applying the KV cache budget scheme optimized on the Needle-in-a-Haystack (NIAH) dataset using the Llama-3-8B-Instruct model. Notably, even without further adaptation, EvolKV consistently achieves the highest average performance across downstream tasks under low-budget constraints (<math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=128</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>), demonstrating its robust generalization capability in transferring optimized budget allocations from a single dataset to diverse task settings.
Furthermore, the budget configuration at <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=256</annotation></semantics></math> is derived by directly expanding the allocation optimized under <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=128</annotation></semantics></math>, further reinforcing the scalability of EvolKV’s budget allocation results, as discussed in Section <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Comparison Results of KV Cache Budgets Expansion and Optimization ‣ Appendix C Detailed Results of Analysis ‣ EvolKV: Evolutionary KV Cache Compression for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>. This not only emphasizes the method’s efficiency in low-resource settings but also highlights its potential for progressive extension to higher budgets without retraining, offering a compelling advantage in practical deployment scenarios.</p>
</div>
